<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">lumberjacking</ansi>

Timber is a trade. Go out with an axe, fell trees, haul the logs home, then
sell them or saw them into lumber and make something.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Where the trees are ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">The Fernway</ansi>        birch, oak, alder, ash, elm, black walnut
  <ansi fg="yellow">Fernway South</ansi>      the same, and rarely ironwood
  <ansi fg="yellow">Cascade Pass Road</ansi>  pine, spruce, larch, cedar, and rarely yew
  <ansi fg="yellow">Pothole Coulee</ansi>     juniper, pine, willow
  <ansi fg="yellow">Ashwick</ansi>            elm, oak, birch, willow
  <ansi fg="yellow">Marshes</ansi>            willow, alder, cypress
  Other woods grow pine, birch, alder and oak, and deep woods spruce, oak,
  elm and the odd yew or walnut.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ What the wood is for ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">softwood</ansi>   pine, spruce, birch, alder, willow, juniper, cedar, larch,
             cypress: saw into planks and arrow shafts
  <ansi fg="yellow">bow wood</ansi>   ash, elm and yew: split into bow staves
  <ansi fg="yellow">hardwood</ansi>   oak, black walnut, ironwood: saw into boards for shields,
             staves and furniture

Rarer woods are worth more and are harder to fell and to work.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Buying and selling ━━━</ansi>

  Camp-Foreman Bertt at the Cascade Pass lumber camp buys logs and sells
  axes, bow saws and planks. Corwin Ashlade, the Amber Valley woodworker,
  buys bows and bowyer's goods and sells shafts, bowstrings and bows.

